<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Western New Guinea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as West New Guinea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> is the western half of the island of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, administered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> since 1963 and now divided into several Papuan provinces. Ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">East Indies</a> and, from 1949 to 1962, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/netherlands-new-guinea">Netherlands New Guinea</a>, it passed to Indonesia after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Agreement and a disputed vote of selected representatives in 1969, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-free-choice">Act of Free Choice</a>. A separatist movement has continued since the 1960s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/western-new-guinea.jpg" alt="Western New Guinea" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mandavi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LocationWestPapua.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
